{
	"description": "Proposed tool calls labeled for the toolCall sites. target is the redacted one-line card target the engine sees. radius names the rung of the blast-radius ladder (contained, local, broad, irreversible); destroys is whether the call deletes, overwrites or discards data that version control or a reinstall cannot bring back; outside is whether it changes anything outside the workspace. A key is omitted where a reasonable reader could go either way. The gateRadius cut is written on the rung position divided by 3, and the probe splits the classes between local and broad.",
	"site": "toolCall",
	"cases": [
		{
			"tool": "bash",
			"actionClass": "read",
			"target": "ls -la src/",
			"expect": {
